-- title:
--   Fibrewise formal smoothness of a normal relative curve
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero, let $\pi \in O$ be such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is the principal ideal $(\pi)$, and assume the residue field of $O$ is algebraically closed. Let $A$ be a domain equipped with an $O$-algebra structure whose scalar action is faithful (so that $O \to A$ is injective), of finite type over $O$, and integrally closed in its fraction field. Let $L$ be a field that is a fraction field of $O$, and let $K$ be a field carrying compatible $O$-, $L$- and $A$-algebra structures (scalar towers $O \to L \to K$ and $O \to A \to K$) with $A \to K$ injective. Suppose there is $x \in A$ whose image in $K$ is transcendental over $L$ and such that $K$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $L(\mathrm{image\ of}\ x)$ generated by that image. Assume further that the quotient $A/(\pi \cdot 1_A)$ is a domain, is integrally closed, and has Krull dimension at most $1$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $O$ the fibre algebra $\mathfrak p.\mathrm{Fiber}\ A$, the base change of $A$ along $O \to \kappa(\mathfrak p)$, is formally smooth over the residue field $\kappa(\mathfrak p)$. Only formal smoothness of each fibre is asserted, not smoothness or finite presentation.
--
--   This supplies the fibrewise hypothesis of a smoothness-by-fibres criterion for a normal relative affine curve over a discrete valuation ring: the two fibres are the generic one, a normal domain of dimension at most one and finite type over the perfect field $L$, and the special one, $A/\pi A$. It is used in the verification that algebras of invariants attached to rigid charts on modular curves of full level are formally smooth, in the three results on invariants of framed and linked-scalar rigid charts that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_residueField_fiber_of_isIntegrallyClosed_quotient_of_transcendental.lean

